@startuml
title The tool registry instance — one record per build per env, one live, append-only history\n(ChatHealthyToolRegistrySchema)

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Segoe UI
skinparam defaultFontSize 11
skinparam ArrowColor #0b7a75
skinparam ComponentBorderColor #0b7a75
skinparam DatabaseBorderColor #6b7280
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #f3f4f6
skinparam NoteBorderColor #9ca3af

[BUILD\ngenerates the record from source\nat one commit, and validates it\nagainst ChatHealthyToolRegistrySchema] as BUILD

database "Mongo · ChatHealthyConfig.ToolConfiguration\nthe one navigation map · append-only · full history\ntools + routes + pages(members/required_members/completeness)" as COLL {
  [instance{build,commit,env,live:true}\nthe live record for this env\n(e.g. build 2292, commit 55c6060e0, env local)] as LIVE
  [older instances · live:false] as HIST
}

[DEPLOY\nthe ONLY writer.\nOne library function, intended all-or-nothing:\nvalidate -> insert new live ->\nretire the predecessor's live flag\n(the sole field ever mutated)] as DEPLOY

[UniversalNavigator\nreads its env's live record at startup;\na runtime metadata change is a\nnew appended record] as UN

package "Guards" #fbfdfd {
  [Unique partial index\ninstance.env where live=true\n-> the DB refuses a second live] as G1
  [$jsonSchema on the collection\n(ChatHealthyToolRegistrySchema)] as G2
  [Pre-commit scan\nno other writer] as G3
  [Audit sweep\nasserts the history invariant] as G4
}

BUILD -down-> DEPLOY : the validated record
DEPLOY -down-> LIVE : insert new live
DEPLOY -[#9ca3af]right-> HIST : retire the old live flag
UN -up-> LIVE : reads at startup
G1 .up.> COLL
G2 .up.> COLL
G3 .up.> DEPLOY
G4 .up.> COLL

note right of DEPLOY
  The record is a projection of source,
  never a source. Written only by the
  deploying identity; every runtime
  identity reads. History is kept, so
  rollback is redeploying an older build.
end note

note bottom of DEPLOY
  OPEN QUESTION (C3 Q5 / N34) — do not resolve here.
  What makes this two-step write (insert new live +
  retire old live) all-or-nothing? A requirement states
  the property for the byte path; none states the analogue
  for a document written into a live collection. Stage-and-
  swap is the available shape. The "all-or-nothing" above
  is the intended property, not a required-and-enforced one.
end note

note right of LIVE
  SCOPE — this record is authoritative for the live
  TOOL / ROUTE / PAGE map of an environment. It is NOT
  the record of the served DATA generation, which is
  governed separately by ChatHealthyConfig.DBVersions.
  OPEN QUESTION (C4 Q7 / N20): which single control record
  is authoritative for "what is published" — two mechanisms
  in different stores each claim it. Flagged, not resolved.
end note
@enduml
